  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, acc=0.639) uses multimodal + multiprofile + pca_n2000 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted. Key findings so far: multimodal > rna-only (+0.04), multiprofile >> singleprofile (+0.09), avgpool > transformer (+0.04), weighted > concat (+0.02). The two major untested axes are the image encoder (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) and the RNA encoder (pca vs scvi/scgpt). Question: Does a stronger, larger image encoder (ViT-L) improve on ResNet50 while keeping all other settings at their validated optima? Why this experiment: config_025 is a clean single-variable swap (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) from the current best, isolating the image-encoder effect. ViT-L is a substantially larger pretrained model and the image modality already proved valuable, making this the highest-impact untested dimension. With 4 experiments left, confirming or ruling out the image-encoder axis first will guide whether to invest remaining budget in RNA-encoder variants or further fusion/aggregation tweaks."
